- data/vista/recorded, data/vista/demo_patients.json and backend/tests/fixtures/vehu_real_replies.json: replies
  recorded from the public WorldVistA VEHU Docker image (https://hub.docker.com/r/worldvista/vehu), a VistA
  demonstration database with synthetic patients. VistA itself was developed by the U.S. Department of Veterans
  Affairs and is distributed through the VA FOIA release (public-domain U.S. Government work); the WorldVistA
  VEHU source repository (https://github.com/WorldVistA/VistA-VEHU-M) is Apache-2.0 and states that it is
  redacted (CPT codes, First Databank drug data and the VA cipher are removed). The image is marked "not for
  production use". The recorded replies contain only synthetic VEHU records (the SSN field of `ORWPT SELECT` holds the constant placeholder `000000000`, never a real or
  VEHU-generated number).
  Confirm the current terms on those pages before redistributing further; this is not legal advice.
- data/mapping/*.csv: small hand-made lookup tables that reference third-party code systems. See
  data/mapping/README.md for the LOINC, SNOMED CT and RxNorm terms that apply.
